Title: test:clautolisp:windows red since 2.2.72 -- a test leaks the MSYS2 run frame
Status: RESOLVED (clautolisp 2.2.73, MR !261; test:clautolisp:windows
        green on the MR pipeline, job 16533656460, 2026-09-16)
Found: 2026-09-16, while checking the Windows jobs of the MR !260 pipeline
Introduced: clautolisp 2.2.72 (093c6395, fix-msys-paths-alfe-parity) --
            my own test
Related: issues/closed/windows-msys-paths-in-autolisp-load-alfe.issue

SYMPTOM

test:clautolisp:windows (native child pipeline, allow_failure) has
failed on EVERY master pipeline since 093c6395, and passed on the two
before it. allow_failure kept the pipelines green, so nobody saw it.

    PHASE7-FINDFILE-HANDLES-ABSOLUTE-PATHS
      "/c/msys64/tmp/tmpVCVIWLRX-tmp.txt"  does not satisfy PROBE-FILE
    BUILTIN-FILE-PRIMITIVES
      FINDFILE        "/c/tmp/clautolisp-builtins-core-.../sample.txt"
                      is not STRING= "C:/tmp/clautolisp-builtins-core-.../sample.txt"
      FINDTRUSTEDFILE "/c/tmp/.../trusted.txt"  vs  "C:/tmp/.../trusted.txt"

(job 16531846195, pipeline 2853737956.) test:alfe:windows is red on the
same pipelines too, but that is a different thing -- the intermittent
"couldn't rename ... status.txt: Acces refuse" of the mock CAD runtime,
already red before 2.2.72.

CAUSE

SYNCHRONIZE-PROCESS-ENVIRONMENT-DOES-BOTH-HALVES
(autolisp-runtime/tests/pathname-mapping-tests.lisp), added in 2.2.72,
calls SYNCHRONIZE-PROCESS-ENVIRONMENT for real and restores nothing. That
function SETFs *RUN-ENVIRONMENT* to the DETECTED run frame, plus the cwd,
the AutoLISP current directory and the support paths.

On the MSYS2 Windows runner the detected run frame is MSYS2, so every
suite that runs afterwards -- builtins-core included -- renders the paths
it returns in MSYS2 form: FINDFILE answers "/c/tmp/..." where the tests,
written for the build frame the test image otherwise keeps, expect
"C:/tmp/...". On Linux and macOS the run frame is the identity, which is
why no local run could show it.

This is a test defect, not an engine one: the clautolisp and alfe
executables call the function once at startup, which is its purpose.

FIX

The test binds *RUN-ENVIRONMENT*, *DEFAULT-PATHNAME-DEFAULTS*,
*AUTOLISP-CURRENT-DIRECTORY* and *AUTOLISP-SUPPORT-PATHS* around its body,
so the calls it makes stay inside it. clautolisp SBCL and CCL: 34 suites
each, 0 failures. The proof that matters is Windows-only: the MR
pipeline's test:clautolisp:windows.

LESSON

A lane that is allow_failure is invisible in exactly the way the old CCL
lanes were (ccl-test-lanes-cannot-fail.issue): its red does not reach the
pipeline status. Check the native child's JOBS, not only its status.
